# A causal loop: CTA c runs c trips, so the count is %ctaid.x and the
# guard skipping CTA 0 is the loop's entry. Per CTA the totals are
# exact in %ctaid.x; over the launch they are unknown, the trips
# differing by CTA, where on an RTX 4090 with 4 CTAs the barrier runs
# 192 times.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cta_trips.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=REC "%s"
CHECK: trips = %ctaid.x
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: bar.sync{{ +}}32 * %ctaid.x{{ +}}%ctaid.x{{$}}
REC: totals per launch [static]:
REC: bar.sync{{ +}}0 + unknown{{ +}}0 + unknown{{$}}
REC: $L__BB0_2  unchecked
